.TH IMUD\-SIGNALK.CONF 5 "2026-08-28" "imud 1.9.0" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
imud\-signalk.conf \- configuration file for imud-signalk(8)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/imud/imud-signalk.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configuration for the
.BR imud-signalk (8)
bridge daemon, which reads imud's binary stream socket and emits Signal K delta
JSON over UDP and/or an optional TCP listener serving the same deltas
newline-framed to connecting clients.  The daemon runs whenever
.B enabled
is true and stays healthy under systemd; each output
.RB ( udp_enabled ,\  tcp_enabled )
is independent and off by default, so nothing is sent until you turn one on.
The bridge reads
.B only
this file (never
.IR imud.conf ).
The file is one
.B [imud-signalk]
section of
.IR key " = " value
lines; strings are double-quoted and
.RB \(oq # \(cq
begins a comment.  Requires imud's
.B [stream]
output enabled.
.PP
Keys marked
.B [hot]
are reloaded on
.BR SIGHUP ;
keys marked
.B [restart]
take effect on the next service start.
.SH KEYS
.\" BEGIN GENERATED: config-keys imud-signalk
.TP
.B enabled
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ false )\ [restart]
Run the Signal K bridge daemon.  With it true and every output off the daemon
runs but sends nothing; set it false to not run the bridge at all (it exits
cleanly, so systemd does not restart it).
The shipped configuration file sets it true; false is what applies when
the key is absent altogether.
.TP
.B socket
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq/run/imud/imud-stream.sock\(dq )\ [restart]
imud stream socket to read (match
.I imud.conf
if you changed it there).
.TP
.B udp_enabled
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ false )\ [restart]
Emit deltas over UDP to
.IR dest_addr : dest_port .
.TP
.B dest_addr
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq127.0.0.1\(dq )\ [hot]
Signal K server host: a hostname, a numeric IPv4 or IPv6 address, or a
broadcast address.  Resolved with
.BR getaddrinfo (3).
Before 1.7 this key accepted numeric IPv4 only.
.TP
.B dest_port
.RI ( int ,\ default:\ 10113 )\ [hot]
UDP port; must match the Signal K server's UDP input connection.
.TP
.B rate_hz
.RI ( int ,\ default:\ 10 )\ [hot]
Delta emit rate in Hz; must be greater than zero.
.TP
.B source_label
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dqimud\(dq )\ [hot]
Signal K delta
.B source.label
value.
.TP
.B publish_heave
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ true )\ [hot]
Emit
.B environment.heave
(set false if imud's heave estimator is off).
.TP
.B tcp_enabled
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ false )\ [restart]
Serve the same deltas (newline-framed JSON, one delta per line) on a TCP
listener; the Signal K server consumes it as a TCP client data connection.
Up to 8 clients.  Independent of
.BR udp_enabled ;
enable either or both.
.TP
.B tcp_bind_addr
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq0.0.0.0\(dq )\ [restart]
Listener bind address (numeric IPv4);
.B 127.0.0.1
keeps it host-local.
.TP
.B tcp_port
.RI ( int ,\ default:\ 10113 )\ [restart]
Listener TCP port (TCP namespace of the UDP default).
.\" END GENERATED: config-keys imud-signalk
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud-signalk.conf
This file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imud-signalk (8),
.BR imud.conf (5),
.BR imud (8)
